>Hi,

>I am developing and application using serial communication to a controler
>card and a CRC (checksum) must be attatch to each command before to send it via the

Rolf Aeschbacher has written a CRC calculation program which does 
a CCITT-CRC (routines are built into Psion ROM) and also a CRC-32.
You my contact him via 100116.3357@compuserve.com (IIUR), otherwise
find a link to his pages from Mark Goulds page (Link to there is 
on mine)

>RS232. The CRC is calculated with an XOR over all caracters in the command to be sent.
>Is anyone have an idea on how to calculate this kind of CRC in OPL. There is no XOR
>operaror in OPL!I heard about the system call $298b but I don't know how to use it and

PROC XOR%:(a%,b%)
	LOCAL xor&
	xor&=&cbc333
	RETURN USR(ADDR(xor&),a%,b%,0,0)
ENDP

